## What this PR does / why we need it:
if foreign key is one column of composite primary/unique key.
when you delete/update parent table. we can get more than one rows for the constraint. we need append agg node to make sure only do some action(insert for update) only once for the constraint.  eg:

```
create table f1(a int, b int, c int, primary key(a,b));
insert into f1 values (2,1,1), (2,2,2),(2,3,3);
create table c1(a int primary key, c_a int, c_b int, constraint c1_ck foreign key(c_a) REFERENCES f1(a) on delete CASCADE on update CASCADE);
insert into c1 values (1,2,1),(2,2,2),(3,2,3);
delete from f1 where b=2;   
//here we have 3 rows for  a=2 in f1.   
// in old logic.  that will do update c1 for 3 *3 rows.  that will make some bug. we only want to do it once with 3 rows.  
```

